Subject: [PATCH 281/333] [ae-patch] Fix the fix-check findings on the queued
 Compact safe point

Fix-check fixes to the previous patch (2026-11-01).

A user_message block without content made isPrepareMessage throw
(JSON.stringify(undefined) has no includes) inside advance() after the phase
was set to preparing but before any timer was armed, so the plan could sit
in preparing forever, and the web test run exited 1 on an unhandled
rejection while "still sees a failure when the transcript is replaced by a
shorter one mid-turn" passed vacuously. A block with no content is now not a
prepare message, both timers are armed before the send-time snapshot, and the
quiet timer catches a rejected advance() and fails the plan with a toast. The
test's fixtures get content and it asserts the failure toast again.

The anchor must follow the newest block at send time, matched by object or
by server item id so a rehydrate keeps it: an older compact's prepare
message loaded by scrolling back while this plan's message is in flight is
no longer taken for the anchor. A prepare message that lands only after its
own turn's idle edge (a late consumed event or snapshot merge) now counts
once a turn ran and a completed response_end follows it, instead of waiting
out the 15 minute limit. New tests cover a contentless user message, the
scrolled-back prepare message, the late landing, and a prepare message that
lands while its turn is already running.
